# HTML & CSS Website – IT Coursework

## Overview

This website was created as part of my IT Coursework 2. The purpose of the project was to design and develop a website that was suitable for a specific target audience.

The target audience for my website was 18–24 year olds, so I focused on creating a modern, interactive and visually appealing design.

## Live Website

[View the live website](https://firrstcar.netlify.app)


## Technologies Used

- HTML
- CSS

## What I Did

I developed the website from the ground up using HTML and CSS.

I personally:

- Built the structure and layout of the website
- Created and customised the colour scheme
- Designed the pages to be consistent throughout
- Added interactive elements
- Adjusted the design specifically for an 18–24 year old audience
- Focused on making the website feel smooth and easy to navigate

## Design & Target Audience

A major part of the project was making sure the website suited its intended audience.

I considered the visual style, colours, layout and interactive features when designing the website for 18–24 year olds. The aim was to create something that felt modern and engaging rather than overly formal.

## What I'm Proud Of

I am particularly proud of the fluidity of the website and how well the different sections work together.

I also think I successfully adapted the design to specifically target a younger audience. This required me to think about how design choices could affect the way different users interact with the website.

## What I Learned

This project improved my understanding of HTML and CSS and gave me more experience designing a website around a specific user group.

It also helped me understand the importance of user experience, consistency and making design decisions based on the target audience rather than simply personal preference.

## Reflection

This project gave me practical experience in web development and strengthened my interest in IT. It showed me that I enjoy building and troubleshooting digital projects and finding ways to improve how users interact with them.
